+## The ActiveMQ broker won't start, or a service can't connect to it
+
+Both of the broker's connectors — STOMP on 61613 and OpenWire on 61616 — require
+mutual TLS, so the Policy Management backend needs a key store and a trust store
+to start the broker at all, and every client needs its own certificate to connect.
+An error naming `certs/policy-management-backend.p12`, a
+`java.nio.file.NoSuchFileException`, or a handshake failure such as
+`Empty client certificate chain` almost always means the development certificates
+have not been generated yet. Run `bash ./generate-certificates.sh` in the
+repository root and start the services again.
+
